+**Where the fields live at consumption:** the player carries `skills: list[dict]` on `SpatialEntity` (`spatial_engine.py:577`); each skill dict is the `Skill.model_dump()`. So consumption is `skill.get("commitment_bin")`, `skill.get("cast_time")`, etc. — the same `skill.get(...)` pattern the existing player-action phase uses (`spatial_engine.py:2375-2377, 2414`). The additive-nullable contract means `.get()` returns `None` on exempt/pre-E4 slots → degenerate path → byte-identical.
