+
+## §2 — The cast-state machine (the new sim primitive; addendum §B.1) — actor-level, on the player entity
+
+### §2.1 — State + carrier fields (new on `SpatialEntity`, additive-defaulted, brownfield-safe)
+
+The state machine is ONE actor-level machine on the player. New defaulted fields on `SpatialEntity` (defaults = the degenerate/idle state → every non-player construction + every pre-E4 fight byte-identical, mirroring the `allegiance`/`cadence_scale` defaulted-field pattern at `:610-636`):
+
+```
+commit_state: str = "idle"          # idle | committing (wind-up) | channeling
+commit_skill_idx: int = -1          # the skill in flight
+commit_started_at: float = 0.0      # elapsed at initiation
+commit_resolve_at: float = 0.0      # elapsed at wind-up completion (committing only)
+channel_next_tick_at: float = 0.0   # elapsed of the next scheduled tick (channeling only)
+channel_tick_n: int = 0             # tick index for ramp (channeling only); reset on break
+channel_origin_x: float = 0.0       # cached placement footprint for tick_tracking=="fixed"
+channel_origin_y: float = 0.0
+commit_lockout_until: float = 0.0   # forced-break recovery lockout (no re-initiate before this)
+_recent_damage_ring: list = []      # trailing (elapsed, dmg) for forced-break window W
+# telemetry accumulators (per-fight, §5):
+committed_completions: int = 0; committed_initiations: int = 0   # → completion_rate/whiff_rate
+channel_ticks_landed: int = 0; channel_ticks_scheduled: int = 0  # → c_chan
+damage_taken_while_committed: float = 0.0
+forced_break_count: int = 0; move_cancel_count: int = 0
+drain_exhaustion_events: int = 0
+channel_activations: int = 0; channel_ticks_delivered_sum: int = 0  # → sustain_uptime / forced_break_rate
+```
+
+**Semantic-shift note (Disc #12):** `action_available_at` (`:680`) gains a NEW meaning during commitment. Pre-E4 it is the sole cadence gate: `if elapsed >= action_available_at` → free to act. Post-E4, while `commit_state != "idle"` the actor is BUSY: the readiness gate must ALSO check the busy-state, not just the cooldown. This is the "readiness gate gains a busy-state" of addendum §B.1. Framed explicitly, NOT buried: the gate now reads "ready = cooldown-elapsed AND not-committed AND not-locked-out." On exempt/snap slots the machine never leaves idle, so the busy-state is inert → byte-identical.
+
+### §2.2 — wind-up: `idle → committing(cast_time) → resolve-at-completion`
+
+At the player action phase (`:2372`), when the selected skill's `commitment_bin == "wind-up"`:
+1. **Initiate** (only if the pilot floor §3 permits): set `commit_state="committing"`, `commit_skill_idx=idx`, `commit_resolve_at = elapsed + cast_time`. **Pay-on-commit** (`pay_on_commit==True`): deduct energy NOW (the existing decrement at `:2436` / `_spend_economy_pool` at `:2433`, moved to initiation). Set cooldown at initiation too (`action_available_at = elapsed + cooldown`, as today at `:2416`) so cadence composes with the commitment leg per the period model `period = k·cooldown + cast_time`. `committed_initiations += 1`.
+2. **In flight** (`committing`, `elapsed < commit_resolve_at`): the actor does NOT select a new skill (busy-state). Wind-up is **un-interruptible at v1** (dispatch §2.6) — incoming damage does NOT break it (only a move-cancel §2.5 or fight-truncation ends it early).
+3. **Resolve at completion** (`elapsed >= commit_resolve_at`): run `_compute_aoe_hits(player, alive_mobs, skill, geo)` against the CURRENT `alive_mobs` positions (`:2386`), then `_apply_skill_damage(...)` (`:2402`). **Motion-whiff is native**: `_compute_aoe_hits` reads live `target.x/target.y` at call time (verified `:842-867` dispatches to `_compute_*_hits` which test live positions), so a wind-up whose template is empty at completion (targets moved out) resolves ZERO hits = a WHIFF. If `len(targets_hit) >= 1`: `committed_completions += 1` (a completion). Else: whiff (no completion increment; the cost is already forfeit by pay-on-commit). Return to `idle`.
+
+**Whiff resolution is EXACTLY the design law (§2.7):** damage resolves against world positions at completion time; the cost is paid at initiation and forfeit on whiff; `completion_rate = committed_completions / committed_initiations`, `whiff_rate = 1 − completion_rate`. NO velocity field needed — I resolve against the actual live positions the world integrated over the cast window (§3 pins how the pilot floor PROJECTS competently).
+
+### §2.3 — channel: `idle → channeling(tick loop) → released | broken | exhausted`
+
+When `commitment_bin == "channel"`:
+1. **Initiate**: `commit_state="channeling"`, `channel_tick_n=0`, `channel_next_tick_at = elapsed` (first tick fires this tick or next scheduled), cache `channel_origin_x/y = player.x/player.y` (for `tick_tracking=="fixed"`). `channel_activations += 1`. Cooldown gate set at initiation. NO pay-on-commit (`pay_on_commit==False`); the channel pays per tick via drain.
+2. **Per tick** (`elapsed >= channel_next_tick_at`): 
+   - **Drain** (`pay_on_commit==False`): debit `drain_rate * tick_interval_seconds` from `player.energy` (per-tick share of the per-second `drain_rate`, HONORED AS-EMITTED). If `player.energy` would go `< 0`: this is **exhaustion** → `drain_exhaustion_events += 1`, transition to `idle` (the natural sustain-window bound, `sustain_window = pool / net_drain`). Do NOT deliver a tick the pool can't fund.
+   - **Resolve the tick**: hit-test per `tick_tracking`. `tracking` → `_compute_aoe_hits(player, alive_mobs, skill, geo)` against live positions (beam re-resolves). `fixed` → hit-test the CACHED footprint at `(channel_origin_x, channel_origin_y)` against current mob positions (tether — targets can walk out). `channel_ticks_scheduled += 1`; if ≥1 hit lands: `channel_ticks_landed += 1`.
+   - **Ramp reward**: the tick's damage is scaled by `ramp(n) = min(1.0, ramp_floor + (1 − ramp_floor)·(channel_tick_n / ramp_n_ticks))`. Apply the ramp as a per-tick `damage_multiplier` scalar into `_apply_skill_damage` (the tick's per-tick damage share, ramp-shaped). `channel_tick_n += 1`; `channel_next_tick_at += tick_interval_seconds`; `channel_ticks_delivered_sum += 1`.
+3. **Voluntary release** (dispatch §2.5): free, any tick boundary — when the hold-logic (§3) says release (target death / no valid target). Return to `idle`; remaining sustain unspent.
+4. **Forced break** (§2.4): the trailing-damage ring fires → break.
+5. **Exhaustion**: pool empty (above).
+
+### §2.4 — Forced-break RULE v1 (F-1b RATIFIED; addendum §C.2; consumed AS-EMITTED)
+
+The trailing-damage ring (`_recent_damage_ring`) accumulates `(elapsed, dmg)` at every incoming-damage site (the player-hp-decrement at `:2577`). At each channel tick, evict entries older than `elapsed − forced_break_window_s` (W=1.0s), then:
+
+```
+Σ(dmg in trailing W)  ≥  forced_break_pct · player.max_hp    ⟹   FORCED BREAK
+```
+
+On forced break: `commit_state="idle"`, `channel_tick_n = 0` (RAMP RESET — F-2b; the teeth), `commit_lockout_until = elapsed + forced_break_lockout_s` (0.4s), the in-flight tick is FORFEIT (no refund — drain already paid, damage not delivered), `forced_break_count += 1`. The lockout blocks re-initiation until `elapsed >= commit_lockout_until` (checked in the readiness busy-state §2.1).
+
+**O(1) per tick:** the ring is a trailing window over `⌈W / tick_size⌉` incoming-damage events; eviction + sum is bounded (§13.2 co-sign — no perf concern). It is populated only when the player is channeling (I gate the append on `commit_state == "channeling"` to keep the non-channel path allocation-free).
+
+**Wind-up is un-interruptible at v1:** the ring does NOT break a `committing` wind-up (dispatch §2.6). The ring only fires during `channeling`.
+
+### §2.5 — Move-cancel (wind-up) + move-policy (channel; addendum §B.4)
+
+- **Wind-up move-cancel**: if the pilot floor would need to reposition (target fled beyond a repositioning threshold) DURING a committing wind-up, the wind-up is CANCELLED: `commit_state="idle"`, cost already forfeit (pay-on-commit), `move_cancel_count += 1`, NO completion. This is the "active whiff-avoidance skill" (addendum §B.5) — but at v1 the competent pilot floor (§3) rarely triggers it because it only initiates when the projected position is inside the template. It exists as a legal transition + a telemetry counter.
+- **Channel move-policy** consumed at the player-navigation branch (`:2289-2360`):
+  - `rooted` (default beams/tethers): **SUSPEND the navigation branch** while `channeling` — the player does not advance toward the target (the lock exposure). The kiting/navigation the branch does is real, so the suspended exposure is real (addendum §B.1). `damage_taken_while_committed` accrues genuinely because the rooted channeler stops repositioning out of danger.
+  - `walk`: scale `movement_speed` by `move_policy_walk_pct` while channeling (the branch runs at reduced speed).
+  - `full_move`: leave the branch untouched (spin class — B12 re-cert target + dodger×channel resolution). The channeler navigates at full speed while channeling.
+
+---
+
+## §3 — Pilot-competence floor v1 (F-competence; addendum §C.4; criterion 18) — the counter-direction threat
+
+The action policy today (`_select_skill_for_entity` + the cast at `:2372-2416`) is commitment-blind: it fires the fastest-cycling affordable skill under kills-only timeout semantics. A blind pilot initiates wind-ups against departing targets → pessimistic completion → inflated premium → over-banded. The v1 floor:
+
+### §3.1 — wind-up initiation gate: project via the motion model (§13.7 — NO velocity field)
+
+**The sim stores no velocity vector** (§13.7 co-sign, grep-verified: no `vx/vy` on `SpatialEntity`; motion is per-tick displacement toward `nav_target`, `:2345-2351`). So the floor FORWARD-INTEGRATES the SAME motion model over the cast window:
+
+```
+project_target_position(target, cast_time):
+    steps = round(cast_time / tick_size)
+    (px, py) = (target.x, target.y)
+    for _ in range(steps):
+        # re-run the mob navigation model (_navigate_entity toward its nav_target == player)
+        (px, py) = one_step_of_mob_motion(target, toward=player_pos, tick_size)
+    return (px, py)
+```
+
+Then: **initiate the wind-up ONLY when the projected `(px,py)` at completion is inside the skill's template** (test the projected point against the geometry footprint via the same `_compute_*_hits` geometry the resolution uses). This is the "one extrapolation" the addendum names, computed against the LIVE motion model so the floor projects the SAME trajectory the world moves on (§13.7 — a projection/resolution split would bias `c_wind`).
+
+**Why the same model matters (Disc #11):** if the floor projected a straight line but the world curved (soft-collision, leash, gather), the measured `c_wind` would be the wrong number — it must be the competent-floor rate rocket prices against, not an idiot-floor OR a clairvoyant-floor rate. Using the actual `_navigate_entity` step keeps it competent-not-clairvoyant: the floor knows the model, not the RNG.
+
+**Cost bound:** `steps = round(cast_time / tick_size)`. At `cast_time = 0.8s`, `tick_size = 0.1s` → 8 projection steps per initiation candidate. Wind-up initiations are sparse (one per period ≈ 13.6s). Negligible vs the per-tick navigation of all mobs. Perf-safe (§8).
+
+### §3.2 — channel hold logic
+
+Hold the channel until: drain exhaustion (§2.3), a threat threshold, or target death — no frivolous release. **Threat threshold**: if the trailing-damage ring is near the forced-break threshold AND `move_policy != rooted`, the competent pilot may voluntarily release + reposition (avoiding the forfeit-tick sting of a forced break). At v1 the minimal competent hold = "hold until target death or exhaustion or forced-break"; the near-threshold voluntary release is the F-competence refinement (implemented as: release if trailing-ring ≥ 0.8·threshold AND move_policy allows repositioning). This keeps the channel-lock exposure REAL (a rooted channeler cannot escape → forced break fires → measured) while a mobile channeler expresses competent play.
+
+### §3.3 — the blind-vs-competent delta report (criterion 18 — the calibration-honesty receipt)
+
+I run the cert gauntlet TWICE per certified kit: once with the **blind pilot** (commitment-blind, initiate-always) and once with the **competent floor** (§3.1/§3.2). Report `Δc_wind = c_wind_competent − c_wind_blind` per (kit, regime). This is the receipt that rocket's priced `c_wind` is the COMPETENT rate, not the idiot rate. Expected sign: `Δc_wind > 0` in mobility regimes (the floor avoids doomed initiations → higher completion). A near-zero delta in a mobility regime would signal the floor isn't projecting (a bug); a large delta confirms the floor is doing real work.
+
+---
+
+## §4 — Capstone expressed-coordinate cert (§3.7; dispatch §6, §10)
+
+T4 capstones declare `(commitment_bin, capstone_amplitude_delta ∈ {none, flatten, invert})`. Cert fires at the EXPRESSED coordinate:
+- `invert` FLIPS the expressed amplitude (spiky↔flat): cert measures the POST-T4 expressed coordinate (`capstone_expressed_amplitude`), not the native.
+- `flatten` / `none` do NOT flip — cert confirms the DECLARED delta whichever it is, never assumes `invert` (§6 amendment — gandalf CONCUR fold).
+- **Declaration-vs-measured mismatch = cert FAIL** (substrate votes). My cert records native + expressed (the cert record carries both — precedent K13→K12 fold). I consume `capstone_expressed_amplitude` as the cert-target coordinate; if my MEASURED expressed amplitude (from the realized damage distribution) disagrees with the declared `capstone_expressed_amplitude`, the kit FAILS cert.
+
+I do NOT re-price the premium; I MEASURE the expressed coordinate and gate on the declaration match.
+
