+## §6 — Three-honesty-axes regime matrix (criterion 17; addendum §C.3) — composition, not new machinery
+
+The pricing loop consumes rates measured across ≥1 regime per honesty axis. The substrate ALREADY EXISTS (verified §13.1 co-sign):
+
+| Honesty axis | Regime property (in-sim) | Prices |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Mobility** | targets that reposition (kite/hit-and-run branch `_navigate_entity` `:1129-1167`) | wind-up whiff rate |
+| **Lethality** | incoming damage that threatens (deaths + HP<50%-timeout losses, `:2577` decrement + fitness-visible) | channel lock exposure + forced-break rate |
+| **Attrition** | fights long enough that sustain windows bind (60–240s scenarios `:70-86`) | drain economics |
+
+The cert matrix is a COMPOSITION requirement: the gauntlet must carry ≥1 of each. I select regimes from the existing scenario catalog + cohort archetypes so that each certified kit's regime composition demonstrably carries ≥1 mobility + ≥1 lethality + ≥1 attrition (the honesty-axes law applies to the cert matrix itself, §6/§4 dispatch). Pricing derives ONLY from the certified mix (guard 2 as LAW — measuring only against stationary targets is dishonest and reopens the spiky-caster over-reward concern).
