+## §7 — Fight-completion floor guard (G-A4; dispatch §0, §6; §13.6 co-sign) — a sim-only guard
+
+Cert asserts the **slowest modulated skill completes ≥2 casts** in a representative gauntlet fight, else the kit flags **dead-slot**. rocket's math note ASSERTS the arithmetic ceiling (§7 constraint 2: period 23.2s → `1 + ⌊30/23.2⌋ = 2` in a 30s fight); MY cert MEASURES the realized cast count of the slowest modulated skill and flags dead-slot if `< 2`. Only my instrument sees a wind-up that prices fine but never fires. Implementation: track per-skill realized-completion counts over a representative fight; the min over modulated skills < 2 → dead-slot flag on the cert record.
